      "why": "Primary feasible candidate: 1 result/cycle throughput with register-every-m stages allows high Fmax to meet 400 MSPS while keeping area lower than fully pipelined. m=2..8 spans the latency/area/Fmax trade-off. data_width 14..20 and n_iter 12..20 cover the accuracy region for max_abs_err <= 2^-12 (accuracy_bits >= 12). Rounding='round' minimizes error for a given n_iter, helping meet the accuracy constraint with fewer iterations/LUTs. angle_guard 0..2 and frac_guard 0..2 keep the angle path and datapath tight to minimize LUTs while preserving accuracy."
    }
